Satoshi (fetched to src/lib/theme/fonts/Satoshi-Variable.woff2)

Satoshi, by Indian Type Foundry. Distributed through Fontshare
(https://www.fontshare.com/fonts/satoshi) under the ITF Free Font License,
which is not an open source licence and is not this project's MIT licence.

The font file is not in this repository or in its history. `npm run fonts`
fetches it from Fontshare per machine, `.gitignore` keeps it untracked, and
`npm run verify:source` fails if any font is committed again. A build then
insists on it: `npm run build` stops rather than produce a bundle without it,
because a downloaded copy of Sill can only carry the face that was on disk
when it was built.

Section 01 of that licence permits embedding the font in a desktop
application, which is what a built copy of Sill does. Section 02 forbids
making the Font Software available through "another font website, font
library, marketplace, repository, download service, application or platform
[...] publicly accessible servers". A git repository is a channel of exactly
that kind: anyone who can clone it can take the file back out and use it on
its own, which is not what section 01 granted.

This repository is private, so keeping the file out of it is a precaution and
not a remedy for anything. It is arranged this way so the answer does not have
to change on the day it stops being private, and so that a fork fetches its own
copy direct from Fontshare and is bound by the licence in its own right, which
is the arrangement the licence describes.

