Menu glyphs in src/lib/components/LauncherMenu.svelte and
src/routes/traymenu/+page.svelte

Phosphor Icons, regular weight (https://phosphoricons.com).

Copyright (c) 2023 Phosphor Icons.
Licensed under the MIT License.

Vendored as path data rather than taken as a dependency: a package would pull a
build step and a tree-shaking question for drawings that change about never,
and the lookup an extension row does on every keystroke is a frozen object.
Vendoring does not shorten the licence, so the notice lives here.

Two places use it. The tray and launcher menus carry a handful of paths inline.
`src/lib/components/marks.ts` carries 296 of them, which is what Raycast's 469
icon names resolve to once the ones that are the same picture are folded
together, so an extension asking for any name Raycast publishes gets a drawing
rather than a letter on a tile.

